2026-10-28T17:30:20.2697809Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016FNUUcedqWMLaaGQ6rKX7T","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 17,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/17\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_db_proxy_default_target_group: removing init_query is never applied (perpetual diff)\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\nTerraform 1.15.x / hashicorp/aws 6.58.0 (code on `main` has the same logic)\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- `aws_db_proxy_default_target_group`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nRemoving `init_query` from `connection_pool_config` (or setting it to `\\\"\\\"`) should clear the initialization query on the RDS Proxy default target group, and the following `terraform plan` should show no changes.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`terraform apply` succeeds, but the initialization query remains set on the target group (confirmed with `aws rds describe-db-proxy-target-groups`). Every subsequent `terraform plan` shows the same in-place update (`init_query: \\\"SET ...\\\" -> null`), i.e. a perpetual diff.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\nNo error output. terraform apply completes successfully.\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand configuration</summary>\\n\\n```hcl\\n# step 1\\nresource \\\"aws_db_proxy_default_target_group\\\" \\\"test\\\" {\\n  db_proxy_name = aws_db_proxy.test.name\\n\\n  connection_pool_config {\\n    init_query = \\\"SET x=1, y=2\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n# step 2: remove init_query and apply\\nresource \\\"aws_db_proxy_default_target_group\\\" \\\"test\\\" {\\n  db_proxy_name = aws_db_proxy.test.name\\n\\n  connection_pool_config {}\\n}\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. `terraform apply`\\n2. Remove `init_query`, `terraform apply` (succeeds)\\n3. `aws rds describe-db-proxy-target-groups --db-proxy-name <name>` still shows `InitQuery`\\n4. `terraform plan` shows the removal again\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nClaude Code (Anthropic) was used to investigate the provider source and draft this report. The reproduction and the AWS CLI verification were performed manually.\\n\\n### Important Facts and References\\n\\n`expandConnectionPoolConfiguration` only sets `InitQuery` when the value is non-empty:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rds/proxy_default_target_group.go\\n\\n```go\\nif v, ok := tfMap[\\\"init_query\\\"].(string); ok && v != \\\"\\\" {\\n    apiObject.InitQuery = aws.String(v)\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`ModifyDBProxyTargetGroup` treats an omitted `ConnectionPoolConfig.InitQuery` as \\\"no change\\\", so the query is never cleared. Sending an empty string is required to clear it. Verified with the AWS CLI:\\n\\n```console\\n$ aws rds modify-db-proxy-target-group --db-proxy-name <name> --target-group-name default \\\\\\n    --connection-pool-config 'MaxConnectionsPercent=100,MaxIdleConnectionsPercent=50,ConnectionBorrowTimeout=120,InitQuery=\\\"\\\"'\\n# response shows \\\"InitQuery\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n$ aws rds describe-db-proxy-target-groups --db-proxy-name <name> --query 'TargetGroups[0].ConnectionPoolConfig'\\n# InitQuery is no longer present\\n```\\n\\n`session_pinning_filters` has the same `v.Len() > 0` guard and presumably the same symptom.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nYes\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [\n10\t    \"bug\"\n11\t  ],\n12\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:36Z\",\n13\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-07T02:36:11Z\"\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8114eea-c71c-477f-a1e0-1b2f0c9f3d5d","uuid":"51d44d85-e48f-4046-885d-7dc41f71b721","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:30:20.265Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 17,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/17\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_db_proxy_default_target_group: removing init_query is never applied (perpetual diff)\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\nTerraform 1.15.x / hashicorp/aws 6.58.0 (code on `main` has the same logic)\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- `aws_db_proxy_default_target_group`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nRemoving `init_query` from `connection_pool_config` (or setting it to `\\\"\\\"`) should clear the initialization query on the RDS Proxy default target group, and the following `terraform plan` should show no changes.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`terraform apply` succeeds, but the initialization query remains set on the target group (confirmed with `aws rds describe-db-proxy-target-groups`). Every subsequent `terraform plan` shows the same in-place update (`init_query: \\\"SET ...\\\" -> null`), i.e. a perpetual diff.\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\nNo error output. terraform apply completes successfully.\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand configuration</summary>\\n\\n```hcl\\n# step 1\\nresource \\\"aws_db_proxy_default_target_group\\\" \\\"test\\\" {\\n  db_proxy_name = aws_db_proxy.test.name\\n\\n  connection_pool_config {\\n    init_query = \\\"SET x=1, y=2\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n# step 2: remove init_query and apply\\nresource \\\"aws_db_proxy_default_target_group\\\" \\\"test\\\" {\\n  db_proxy_name = aws_db_proxy.test.name\\n\\n  connection_pool_config {}\\n}\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. `terraform apply`\\n2. Remove `init_query`, `terraform apply` (succeeds)\\n3. `aws rds describe-db-proxy-target-groups --db-proxy-name <name>` still shows `InitQuery`\\n4. `terraform plan` shows the removal again\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nClaude Code (Anthropic) was used to investigate the provider source and draft this report. The reproduction and the AWS CLI verification were performed manually.\\n\\n### Important Facts and References\\n\\n`expandConnectionPoolConfiguration` only sets `InitQuery` when the value is non-empty:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rds/proxy_default_target_group.go\\n\\n```go\\nif v, ok := tfMap[\\\"init_query\\\"].(string); ok && v != \\\"\\\" {\\n    apiObject.InitQuery = aws.String(v)\\n}\\n```\\n\\n`ModifyDBProxyTargetGroup` treats an omitted `ConnectionPoolConfig.InitQuery` as \\\"no change\\\", so the query is never cleared. Sending an empty string is required to clear it. Verified with the AWS CLI:\\n\\n```console\\n$ aws rds modify-db-proxy-target-group --db-proxy-name <name> --target-group-name default \\\\\\n    --connection-pool-config 'MaxConnectionsPercent=100,MaxIdleConnectionsPercent=50,ConnectionBorrowTimeout=120,InitQuery=\\\"\\\"'\\n# response shows \\\"InitQuery\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n$ aws rds describe-db-proxy-target-groups --db-proxy-name <name> --query 'TargetGroups[0].ConnectionPoolConfig'\\n# InitQuery is no longer present\\n```\\n\\n`session_pinning_filters` has the same `v.Len() > 0` guard and presumably the same symptom.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nYes\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"bug\"\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:36Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-07T02:36:11Z\"\n}","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016FNUUcedqWMLaaGQ6rKX7T","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
